# 5. OFFICIAL INSURANCE CHECK FUNCTIONALITY

This is the most important technical requirement.

The application must NOT pretend to have direct access to the Motor Insurance Database (MID) or Navigate database.

There must be:

- No fake insurance results.
- No simulated insured/uninsured results.
- No invented insurance APIs.
- No fabricated policy details.
- No fake database connection.
- No misleading claims of real-time verification.

Official authority:

Motor Insurers' Bureau (MIB).

Official information page:

https://www.mib.org.uk/check-and-stay-insured/check-your-vehicle/

Use this official MIB page as the external destination for the checking process.

Keep the destination URL in one central configuration file so it can be updated later.

Do not invent or assume that the external service accepts registration numbers through URL parameters.

The user must complete the actual insurance check on the official MIB website.

## Official checking rules

Clearly explain:

- The free public service is for checking a vehicle the user owns or has the legal right to drive.
- Users must follow the official service's terms and conditions.
- A result showing insured means a live policy exists against that vehicle.
- It does not guarantee that the policy covers every type of use.
- Newly purchased or renewed insurance may take several days to appear.
- If the result appears incorrect, the user should contact their insurer.

Do not suggest that the public checker can be used to investigate any unrelated vehicle.

## User journey

Step 1: User visits the website.

Step 2: User enters a UK vehicle registration number.

Step 3: Application validates the input format.

Step 4: Application displays a confirmation panel.

Step 5: User copies the registration number if necessary.

Step 6: User clicks "Continue to Official MIB Check".

Step 7: Open the official MIB service in a new tab.

Step 8: User completes the actual insurance check on the official website.

